+An **integrity failure** is one of immudb's sentinels: `ErrCorruptedData` (inclusion or dual proof failed, or the server could not read stored data), `ErrCorruptedTxData` (the server's stored transaction does not hash — an ALH mismatch — or cannot be read), `ErrServerStateIsOlder` (the server is behind the client's trusted state), `ErrServerIdentityValidationFailed` (a different server at the same address), or `ErrLocalStateCorrupted` (the persisted baseline cannot be read). Client-local sentinels match by identity. A server-returned `ErrCorruptedData` or `ErrCorruptedTxData` arrives as a raw gRPC status: immudb v1.11.2 `mapServerError` assigns it no code and no `ErrorInfo`, and `VerifiedGet` does not convert it back to the sentinel. `isIntegrityError` treats `codes.Unknown` or `codes.Internal` as an integrity failure when any `": "`-delimited segment of the status message equals one of those two sentinels' text (`"data is corrupted"` or `"tx data is corrupted"`). The server image pin `codenotary/immudb:1.11.1` uses those same sentences. `TestServerIntegritySentinelText` fails if the pinned SDK rewords either sentence; that failure is the signal to re-check the server image pin in `internal/testimages/testimages.go` and `docker-compose.yml` before updating the matcher. The first time the auditor sees one:
 
